warning: the value bound to `unused` may never be waited for
 --> should_fail/bad-unused.anvil:3:5
  |
3 |     let unused = { cycle 1 >> 1'b1 };
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this value takes time to compute
  = note: after `;` the code continues without waiting for the value, so a path that does not use it can end before the value is ready
  = help: use `>>` instead of `;` to wait for the value, or use it on every path

error: printed value is used before it is available
 --> should_fail/bad-unused.anvil:7:7
  |
7 |       dprint "Value is %d" (unused);
  |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the value is used here
 --> should_fail/bad-unused.anvil:3:20
  |
3 |     let unused = { cycle 1 >> 1'b1 };
  |                    ^^^^^^^ the value is only available after this `cycle 1`
  = help: wait for the value with `>>` before using it, e.g. `let x = ... >> dprint "%d" (x)`

